{
  "version": 40,
  "notes": "Version 40 adds a new technique, social_scraping (\"Social scraping\") on 2026-11-21 (codebook 15): a crowd of unknown size and its reaction reported as the news (\"Fans are furious\", \"People are just realizing\", \"The internet reacts\"), often built from a few social media posts. One new signal, crowd_reaction: a crowd word, optional helpers and a reaction word, left alone for a real count, a named speaker, people in the story stating a fact, a negated claim, a leading quote, shopping copy, first person, a study, poll or bug report, and the writer cheering the reader on. The crowd phrases that sat in vague_sourcing (\"people are saying\", \"many are saying\", \"fans brand\", \"viewers brand\", \"shoppers say\", \"shoppers reveal\", \"customers say\", \"diners say\") move here unchanged, with the same weights.",
